FenrirOS: core's native build against the system's ICU, Boost and OpenSSL and
the euro-office-v8 package, where upstream builds its own (ICU 74, Boost 1.83,
OpenSSL 1.1.1f from Git, by Common/3dParty/build_3rdparty.py, which the
recipe skips with THIRD_PARTY_PREPARED) and copies the ICU libraries next to
x2t.

- ICU: the system's (78) shared libraries, by their unversioned names; the
  ICU copy into the output directory goes (copy_icu_libs, Linux branch).
- Boost: the system's (1.91), through its CMake config (CMP0167 NEW) and as
  shared libraries. Boost.System is header-only since 1.69 and its stub
  library is gone since 1.89, so it is no longer asked for as a component;
  core's targets still link Boost::system, so that becomes an interface target
  for Boost's headers when Boost's config does not define it.
- OpenSSL: the system's (3.x) shared libraries (core already carries the asio
  patch for OpenSSL 3; upstream links 1.1.1f statically).
- V8: /usr/lib/euro-office-v8, where euro-office-v8 installs nc-build.py's
  layout (libv8_monolith.a, v8/include, v8/src).

